## Cross-Phase Feature Correlation Summary

| Feature | CPI MoM | Yield Dir | NFP Change | SPY Regime |
|---------|---------|-----------|-----------|-----------|
| CPI MoM (lag) | **+0.54** | weak | weak | weak |
| Commodities (DBC) | **+0.51** | weak | **+0.42** | weak |
| SPY return | weak | weak | **+0.48** | weak |
| PPI MoM | **+0.46** | weak | **+0.34** | weak |
| Breakeven proxy | +0.29 | +0.28 | weak | weak |
| TLT return | -0.27 | -0.28 | weak | weak |
| HYG return | weak | weak | weak | weak |
| Dollar (UUP) | weak | weak | weak | weak |

**Key insight:** Commodity prices (DBC) are the most cross-cutting predictor — they signal both CPI and NFP. Market-implied inflation (TIPS breakeven) is weaker than commodity prices for predicting actual CPI.

