## Honest Summary

| Phase | Target | Best Model | Sig? | Verdict |
|-------|--------|-----------|------|---------|
| 1 CPI | MoM % | RF -15% RMSE | p=0.19 ✗ | Marginal, unproven |
| 2 NFP | k jobs | RF worse post-COVID | p=0.39 ✗ | No edge (incomplete) |
| 3 Yield | Up/Down | Logit = majority class | p=0.71 ✗ | No edge |
| 4 Regime | SPY regime | RF worse than majority | p=0.84 ✗ | No edge |

**Bottom line:** With free data (BLS + Yahoo Finance monthly), no phase demonstrates a statistically significant predictive edge over the appropriate baseline. The CPI model has the most promise (r=0.54, RF beats naive) but p=0.19 means we cannot rule out noise.

**To unlock real edge, in priority order:**
1. FRED API key (free) → initial claims, 800k+ series
2. Daily data instead of monthly → yield direction becomes tractable
3. ADP Employment (free release, manual scrape) → NFP prediction
4. 5+ more years of data → CPI model significance

